# A PaiNN of 4 features and 2 layers with random weights in stages whose
# bodies are batched (D[ml4-batched-bodies], docs/ml4-ir.md, Section 8.3):
# scripts/mlip/painn-stages.py exports each stage and its jax.vjp to
# StableHLO with 8 rows a tile, legalized to linalg by stablehlo-opt; the
# loops run in tiles on a device, the pairs over the slots of the pairs of
# images. The energy, the forces, and the virial of 27 waters in a cubic
# cell of 1.02 nm (81 atoms) against the same stages in JAX composed with
# the reverse rules of Section 4.1 of the design, in float32 bodies and
# float64 sums (`painn-stages.py harness`), within 1e-5 of the largest
# value. Measured on an RTX 4090: double 0, 2.5e-7, 6.6e-8; mixed 5.5e-9,
# 7.9e-7, 1.9e-7.
#
# REQUIRES: cuda, stages-export
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %jax_python %S/../../scripts/mlip/painn-stages.py weights --synthetic 4 2 %t/w.npz
# RUN: %jax_python %S/../../scripts/mlip/painn-stages.py export %t/w.npz %t/model.mlir --rows 8 --stablehlo-opt %stablehlo_opt --workdir %t
# RUN: %jax_python %S/../../scripts/mlip/painn-stages.py harness %t/w.npz --waters 27 > %t/harness.mlir
# RUN: echo 'md.particle_set @atoms' > %t/head.mlir
# RUN: cat %t/head.mlir %t/model.mlir %t/harness.mlir > %t/m.mlir
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/m.mlir %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_transforms \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-storage="memory=device" --md-exec-lower-stage-bodies \
# RUN:     --convert-md-exec-to-gpu \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_gpu_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/m.mlir %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_transforms \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-precision="mode=mixed" \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-storage="memory=device" --md-exec-lower-stage-bodies \
# RUN:     --convert-md-exec-to-gpu \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_gpu_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s

# The energy, the forces, and the virial agree, each printing 1, and the
# largest difference of each is printed after it.
# CHECK:      {{^}}1{{$}}
# CHECK-NEXT: {{^[0-9.e+-]+$}}
# CHECK-NEXT: {{^}}1{{$}}
# CHECK-NEXT: {{^[0-9.e+-]+$}}
# CHECK-NEXT: {{^}}1{{$}}
# CHECK-NEXT: {{^[0-9.e+-]+$}}
